[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mFor the per-client rate limits in orbit/limits.py, how should a "client" be identified?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mPer API key[39m
     [38;5;246mEach API key gets its own bucket. Fair to shared-IP users (NAT, offices), but needs every request to be authenticated.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Per IP address
     [38;5;246mBucket by client IP. Works for anonymous traffic, but users behind NAT share a limit and a proxy needs X-Forwarded-For handling.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m API key, IP fallback
     [38;5;246mUse the API key when one is present, otherwise fall back to the client IP for unauthenticated requests.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
